# Keep secrets and data out of the build context.
#
# This is not tidiness. `next build` with output:"standalone" copies the
# project directory into .next/standalone, and on this machine that swept up
# .env and data/bot.keystore.json along with 1.8GB of scan databases. Built
# into an image and pushed to a registry, that would have put the API token,
# the keystore passphrase AND the encrypted key itself inside a published
# artifact — both halves of the wallet, in one layer, permanently.
#
# Docker never sees these, so the build cannot copy what is not there.

# ── secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.keystore.json

# ── data: databases are built at runtime on the mounted volume ──────────
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# ── build output and local state ────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
node_modules/
out/
build/
*.log

# ── repo furniture with no place in a runtime image ─────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
docs/
tests/
scripts/
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
